From: HakiOS
Subject: [PATCH] sweet: freeze probe (RedwoodGPU requests in flight, FRZ thread dumps)

A UI freeze: frames stop, the GPU is idle (fence done, 0 ms pending), touches
still arrive, no crash, no panic. In logs/xnu-0101s0-freeze.txt the process
sampler (0054) happened to run 56 s into one: backboardd's CoreAnimation
thread was in mach_msg2_trap under IOConnectCallStructMethod from libOSMesa
msm_bo_new (DRM_MSM_GEM_NEW, selector 0x42) <- fd_bo_new <- realloc_bo <-
st teximage <- glTexImage2D (libOSMesa loaded at 0x107000000; return
addresses matched to BL instructions). Where in the kernel it waits is not
known. This patch makes the next freeze say so in one boot:

- RedwoodGPU.cpp: a table of the requests in flight (selector, size, step of
  gemNew, start time, thread) and gGPULock's holder; redwood_gpu_inflight_ms(),
  redwood_gpu_inflight_report().
- SweetFramebuffer.cpp: the once-a-second line triggers a dump when frames
  had been coming and none came for 4 s while touches arrived, or when a
  request has been in RedwoodGPU for 3 s (8 dumps at most, 20 s apart).
  "SWEET FREEZE: ..." line. Boot-arg sweetfreeze=0: off.
- bsd/dev/sweet_sample.c: sweet_freeze_dump() on a thread of its own: the
  requests in flight (with kernel backtraces), then every thread of
  sweetfreeze_names (default backboardd,SpringBoard).
- osfmk/kern/exception.c: sweet_thread_dump(): state, block hint, wait event,
  priority, user pc/lr/bt, kernel bt from the saved kernel context (unslid).
- hid/SweetHID.cpp: sweet_hid_touches counter.

Applies on xnu/patches 0001..0112 (current series). Untested: not compiled locally.
